feine","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Cannabis","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"DOx","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"MAOIs","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"MDMA","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"MXE","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."}],"citations":[{"title":"Severe clinical toxicity associated with analytically confirmed recreational use of 25I-NBOMe: case series","url":"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/23731373"}],"helpfulLinks":[{"title":"PsychonautWiki","description":"Pharmacology, subjective effects, and dosage reference","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/25I-NBOMe"},{"title":"TripSit Factsheet","description":"Rapid harm-reduction summary and combination data","url":"https://drugs.tripsit.me/25i-nbome"},{"title":"Erowid Experience Vaults","description":"First-person experience reports and archives","url":"https://www.erowid.org/experiences/subs/exp_25INBOMe.shtml"},{"title":"Wikipedia","description":"Encyclopedia article","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/25I-NBOMe"},{"title":"Wikidata","description":"Structured data on 25I-NBOMe","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4632141"}],"wikidata":"Q4632141","pharmacology":{"text":"25I-NBOMe acts as a highly potent full agonist for the human 5-HT2A receptor, with a affinity (Ki) of 0.044 nM, making it some 16-fold higher affinity than 2C-I at this receptor. 25I-NBOMe induces a head-twitch response in mice which is blocked completely by a selective 5-HT2A antagonist, suggesting its psychedelic effects are mediated by 5-HT2A. This study suggested that 25I-NBOMe is approximately 14-fold more potent than 2C-I in-vivo.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"25I-NBOMe","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/25I-NBOMe#Pharmacodynamics","kind":"Serotonin 5-HT2 receptor agonist; Serotonergic psychedelic; Hallucinogen","body":[{"what":"brokenDown","says":"Extensive first-pass metabolism in the liver"},{"what":"leaves","says":"Urine"}],"figures":"25I-NBOMe"},"uses":{"text":"25I-NBOMe is commonly administered sublingually, buccally, and intranasally. For sublingual and buccal administration, 25I-NBOMe is often applied to sheets of blotter paper and held in the mouth to allow absorption through the oral mucosa. There are also reports of intravenous injection of a 25I-NBOMe solution, as well as smoking the drug in powdered form.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"25I-NBOMe","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/25I-NBOMe#Use_and_effects","routes":"Mainly sublingual, buccal, and insufflation","figures":"25I-NBOMe"},"formula":"C18H22INO3","molarMass":427.3}